      "weight_variable_name": null,
      "weight_fields_interpretation": "This paper is a dataset construction/harmonization study rather than an analysis of student microdata from an ILSA sampling frame. The authors construct harmonized country-year educational quality indicators (Tscore_INT/Tscore_ML, Tscore1519_INT/Tscore1519_ML, Q_INT/Q_ML) by mapping TIMSS and PISA scores onto the TIMSS 1995 metric and imputing missing country-year values. Because the unit of analysis is country-year (and the paper does not describe applying ILSA student/sampling weights such as W_FSTUWT or replicate-weight schemes), student-level survey weighting and replicate-weighting are not applicable here. The only explicit weighting mentioned is population weighting in the working-age educational quality index (ages 15–64), which is not an ILSA complex-survey weight for student sampling."
    },
    "plausible_values_handling": "not_applicable",
    "missing_data_handling": "not_reported",
    "handling_not_reported_explanation": "Plausible values (PVs) are not applicable because the study does not analyze ILSA student-level achievement PVs; instead, it constructs harmonized country-year test-score series and imputes missing country-year observations using linear interpolation and LASSO regression. The missing-data handling refers to imputing missing country-year entries in the constructed panel (581 missing values out of 1212 potential country-year observations), but the paper does not describe PV-based multiple imputation or a PV-combining procedure. Therefore, PV handling and PV-related missing-data handling are not applicable to this dataset-construction context.",
