    "outcome_summary": "The study constructs a harmonized cross-country educational quality dataset for 101 countries from 1970 to 2023 by anchoring TIMSS scores to the TIMSS 1995 metric (mean 500, SD 100) and mapping PISA scores via equi-percentile linking. Missing country-year observations (581 of 1212 potential, 48%) are imputed using two approaches: linear interpolation/extrapolation (Tscore_INT) and LASSO-based prediction using 501 World Bank economic/education indicators (Tscore_ML). The LASSO model achieves RMSE = 17.5 and R² = 0.912 on its validation setup (with a 80/20 split and tenfold cross-validation during grid search), and the paper reports out-of-sample performance of RMSE = 15.7 and R² = 0.905 for the imputation task. The authors then derive annual educational quality indicators for ages 15–19 (Tscore1519_INT/Tscore1519_ML) and working-age educational quality indexes for ages 15–64 (Q_INT/Q_ML), using population-weighted aggregation and an estimated return to test scores. The resulting country-year series are used to characterize cross-country patterns in educational quality and its relationship with educational quantity (correlation = 0.67 in 2015).",
